      "writtenOn": "2020-01-29T16:16:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is it possible to expose this via a getter that is also synchronized? You can add @VFT(otherwise \u003d NONE), which indicates that this method shall only be called from test code. Proguard should strip away such methods from production code.\n\nI think member variables of this class are protected by \u0027this\u0027 lock. So accessing this field directly in tests means the appropriate lock won\u0027t be acquired.\n\nSame may probably also apply for mVpnRunner.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 187,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 187,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "dec7a71afe933a74927c1238919400de647b57d0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "51cc0a19_f83543f2",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/Vpn.java",
        "patchSetId": 52
      },
      "lineNbr": 2071,
